@flexiarg snatch/escalate-only-as-far-as-you-can-lose
@title Escalate Only as Far as You Can Lose
@audience players
@tone practical
@style pattern
@why snatch/protect-the-unprotected-move
@see-also snatch/probe-before-committing

! conclusion: After an acceptance, raise the offer by an increment whose seizure you could still absorb.

  + context: **Play grain.** The complement of `probe-before-committing`: what to
    do once the probe has come back favourably.

  + IF:
    A counterpart has accepted an offer, and larger offers are available.

  + HOWEVER:
    One acceptance is weak evidence — a snatcher who accepts once has lost
    nothing by waiting — and an offer sized to the belief rather than to the loss
    turns a good read into an unrecoverable position.

  + THEN:
    Raise the offer by an increment whose seizure you could absorb and still
    continue, and stop raising when you could not.

  + BECAUSE:
    Belief about a counterpart is revisable and a seized token is not. Size the
    exposure to what you can survive being wrong about, not to how right you
    currently feel.
